the video game industry has never been  more innovative or exciting but with so  many great games coming out it's  inevitable that some games would just  slip through the cracks here's a look at  some incredible games no one bought  vampire the masquerade bloodlines hardly  anyone bought vampire the masquerade  bloodlines when it came out over a  decade ago vampires weren't yet  sparkling and the kind of vampires  bloodlines del worth were no longer that  popular but those are did buy the game  are not only still playing it but  creating their own new content for it  that's the kind of passion this hybrid  RPG inspires in its fans of its  immersive story of a vampire who must  negotiate a world of undead clans  competing for supremacy it remains a  great treat for retro gamers but be  careful even now the hotel level is  scary enough to cause my mess so play at  your own risk Panzer Dragoon saga after  to traditional rail shooters the Panzer  Dragoon franchise took an unexpected  detour into the realm of Final Fantasy  style RPGs with this classic 1998  release Panzer Dragoon saga has been  acclaimed as one of the greatest RPGs of  all time  so why didn't anyone buy it well I had  the misfortune of being released for the  Sega Saturn in 1998 the same year the  platform was discontinued in North  America talk about bad timing  psyops the mind gate conspiracy in this  one endured adventure from 2004 for the  Xbox and ps2 players assume control of  an amnesiac of psychic powers and the  nefarious paramilitary group on his tail  it may not sound particularly innovative  now but that's because dozens of games  have since copied its mind-bending  telekinetic gameplay sadly fans of the  game never got a sequel and likely never  will as the studio behind psyops closed  in 2010 deadly premonition lots of games  get mixed reviews but Delly premonition  actually earned the guinness world  record for being the most critically  polarizing survival horror game taking  many cues from Twin Peaks and Japanese  horror Deadly Premonition is a must  played title for fans of B movies and  anyone wanting a bizarre left-field  experience you have to buy gas for your  car without coffee you'll get sleepy on  top of this the graphics aren't even  great for 2010 and the combat system is  terrible in other words it's not for  everyone but if you don't hate it  chances are you're gonna love it  with Deadly Premonition there's really  no middle ground Viking battle for  Asgard there's something to be said for  a game of mindless destruction spent  mowing down enemies like weeds sure it  might not break new ground but if you  want to break some skills instead this  is your game lost in the shuffle among  more hyped and more innovative titles  Viking battle for Asgard just as one  simple thing but it does it very very  well indeed The Saboteur the final game  from developer pandemic studios The  Saboteur is the open-world game set  during world war two sort of like Grand  Theft Auto in german-occupied France  with noir inspired graphics and an  unusual story based style that sees you  inspiring rebellion against the Nazi  overlords The Saboteur feels about as  far from cookie-cutter world war ii  shooters as possible and that's a good  thing  vanquish running gun duck and cover  punched Giants in the face it's not just  the mantra of this fast-paced  third-person shooter it's also a motto  for life vanquish doesn't necessarily do  anything new but it does everything well  with the controls and graphics all  top-notch for a last generation actioner  fans at the time thought it looked too  derivative of games like Bayonetta but  sometimes fun Trump's innovation this is  one of those times brutal legend  designer Tim Schafer previously brought  gamers idiosyncratic titles like  Psychonauts and Grim Fandango and this  is no exception a rock and roll Love  Letter featuring the likes of Ozzy  Osbourne and Lemmy Kilmister from  Motorhead among its voice cast brutal  legend find your roadie player character  and their party roaming across a heavy  metal hellscape securing territory  through real-time combat and strategy  the game while a poor seller was praised  for his wit and charm check it out and  rock on bro singularity singularity is a  first-person shooter with a heady time  manipulation mechanic that allows you to  travel forward and backwards through  time affecting gunplay and the  convoluted plot accused of being a  Bioshock knockoff when it was released  this entertaining romp is still worth a  run through for some memorable moments  and my marish monsters and if you can  find some friends to join you for  multiplayer even better thanks for  watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our youtube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  your love to  you
 

